{
  "version": 1,
  "note": "archon-sdk conformance vectors — the layer above the identity floor: proof of possession and the signed envelope. Every case is stated in the floor's vocabulary plus two fixed byte layouts (ADR 0004): nothing here needs the words root, admission, grant, fact, receipt or epoch. A seed of the wrong size is a refusal in every lane (it comes from custody, not code). Entropy, time and binding are case INPUTS — the sdk never sources them — which is what makes every output deterministic and pinnable.",
